{"id":"04dba9d531bc1aa8","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-thm-koenig-theorem.md","title":"König Theorem","display":"thm-koenig-theorem — König Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-koenig-theorem","aliases":["58-thm-koenig-theorem","König Theorem","König Cardinal Inequality"],"display":"thm-koenig-theorem — König Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-cardinal]]","[[58-df-cardinaladd]]","[[58-df-cardinalmul]]","[[58-df-cardinalexpp]]","[[58-df-cofinality]]","[[58-ax-ac]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-koenig-theorem"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-koenig-theorem</span><span>König Theorem</span><span>König Cardinal Inequality</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-koenig-theorem — König Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"58-df-cardinal\">58-df-cardinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"a1504fbca72b2f04\" href=\"?note=a1504fbca72b2f04\" title=\"58-df-cardinaladd\">58-df-cardinaladd</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"c93bb7bd2c75a2d3\" href=\"?note=c93bb7bd2c75a2d3\" title=\"58-df-cardinalmul\">58-df-cardinalmul</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"949691fe1747f59d\" href=\"?note=949691fe1747f59d\" title=\"58-df-cardinalexpp\">58-df-cardinalexpp</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"315ad00b8744fdfc\" href=\"?note=315ad00b8744fdfc\" title=\"58-df-cofinality\">58-df-cofinality</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"b3dac4cf78c440c7\" href=\"?note=b3dac4cf78c440c7\" title=\"58-ax-ac\">58-ax-ac</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\\in V\">\\(\\kappa\\in V\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\)</span> is the imported cardinal predicate</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cf}(\\kappa)\">\\(\\mathrm{cf}(\\kappa)\\)</span> (cofinality of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CardExp}_S(\\kappa,\\lambda)\">\\(\\mathrm{CardExp}_S(\\kappa,\\lambda)\\)</span> 为基数参数上的二元基数指数函数，见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"949691fe1747f59d\" href=\"?note=949691fe1747f59d\" title=\"58-df-cardinalexpp.md\">58-df-cardinalexpp.md</a>。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}koenig\\text{-}theorem}\\vdash\n\\forall\\kappa\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega\\leq\\kappa\n\\to\\kappa&lt;\\mathrm{CardExp}_S(\\kappa,\\mathrm{cf}(\\kappa))\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}koenig\\text{-}theorem}\\vdash\n\\forall\\kappa\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega\\leq\\kappa\n\\to\\kappa&lt;\\mathrm{CardExp}_S(\\kappa,\\mathrm{cf}(\\kappa))\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>König: proved theorem (1905).</li>\n<li>Generalizes Cantor's theorem.</li>\n<li>Key: cofinality role in exponentiation.</li>\n<li>In full generality, if <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa_i &lt; \\lambda_i\">\\(\\kappa_i &lt; \\lambda_i\\)</span> for all <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"i \\in I\">\\(i \\in I\\)</span>, then <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sum_{i \\in I}\\kappa_i &lt; \\prod_{i \\in I}\\lambda_i\">\\(\\sum_{i \\in I}\\kappa_i &lt; \\prod_{i \\in I}\\lambda_i\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>A standard consequence is <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cf}(2^{\\aleph_0}) &gt; \\aleph_0\">\\(\\mathrm{cf}(2^{\\aleph_0}) &gt; \\aleph_0\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Application: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"2^{\\aleph_0}\">\\(2^{\\aleph_0}\\)</span> cannot be <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_\\omega\">\\(\\aleph_\\omega\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Easton's theorem: shows König's bounds are optimal for regular cardinals.</li>\n<li>Silver's theorem: constraint on singular cardinals.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"5fb1c2241d1943d1","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cardinal]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cardinaladd","status":"resolved","id":"a1504fbca72b2f04","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cardinaladd]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cardinalmul","status":"resolved","id":"c93bb7bd2c75a2d3","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cardinalmul]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cardinalexpp","status":"resolved","id":"949691fe1747f59d","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cardinalexpp]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cofinality","status":"resolved","id":"315ad00b8744fdfc","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cofinality]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-ax-ac","status":"resolved","id":"b3dac4cf78c440c7","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-ax-ac]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cardinalexpp.